          {
            "index": 0,
            "text": "Electrical energy is convenient to transmit, distribute and convert.\nWires can carry it to distant places, where it can be distributed to different users.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 123.734375,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 1,
            "text": "Suitable devices can convert electrical energy into mechanical energy, internal energy, light and other forms.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 213.4375,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 2,
            "text": "A transformer can change the voltage and current of alternating electricity over a wide range.\nAn ideal transformer does not lose energy, but a real transformer does.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 303.140625,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 109.125
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 3,
            "text": "Changing voltage and current is important in many electrical and radio devices, as well as in long-distance power transmission.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 429.21875,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 4,
            "text": "Devices that supply electrical energy convert other forms of energy into electrical energy.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 518.921875,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 5,
            "text": "Examples include batteries, electrostatic generators, thermopiles① and the solar cells used on spacecraft.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 608.625,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 6,
            "text": "A fuel cell can convert the chemical energy released by a reaction between hydrogen and oxygen into electrical energy.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 698.328125,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 7,
            "text": "A magnetohydrodynamic generator uses hot ionized gas, or plasma, flowing through a magnetic field to convert energy of the gas into electrical energy.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 788.03125,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 8,
            "text": "① A thermopile uses the electromotive force produced when junctions made from different materials are at different temperatures.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 877.734375,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 9,
            "text": "The characteristics of each device determine where it is useful.\nAn electrostatic generator can produce a large potential difference, but it supplies only a small current.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 967.4375,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 109.125
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 10,
            "text": "A battery bank can supply a larger current, but its operating time is limited by conditions such as the energy stored in it.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 1093.515625,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 11,
            "text": "An **electromechanical induction AC generator** converts mechanical energy into electrical energy by electromagnetic induction.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 1183.21875,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 12,
            "text": "Its basic principle and structure are relatively simple, and a suitable design can produce the required voltage and supply a large current to a load.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 1272.921875,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
            "border": "0px",
            "indent": "0px"
          },
          {
            "index": 13,
            "text": "In the rest of this chapter, the term “generator” refers to an electromechanical induction AC generator.",
            "rect": {
              "x": 377.59375,
              "y": 1362.625,
              "width": 684.8125,
              "height": 72.75
            },
            "section": false,
